cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use arcgis-mcp-bridge in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
title: "arcgis-mcp-bridge: a secure Model Context Protocol server for ArcGIS Pro"
type: software
authors:
  - name: muend
abstract: >-
  A secure, local-first, asynchronous MCP (Model Context Protocol) server
  exposing ArcGIS Pro's ArcPy geoprocessing engine to large-language-model
  hosts over stdio JSON-RPC. Provides 100 declarative geoprocessing tools
  across 10 GIS verticals, two-process arcpy isolation, PathGuard filesystem
  sandboxing, and Pydantic v2 contract validation in both processes.
keywords:
  - GIS
  - ArcGIS
  - arcpy
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - GeoAI
  - spatial analysis
  - geoprocessing
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/muend/arcgis-mcp-bridge"
url: "https://github.com/muend/arcgis-mcp-bridge"
version: 0.5.0
date-released: 2026-06-11
